I get off the tram in the city centre.
The streets are very busy today.
It is Saturday and many people are out and about.
Outside a bakery stands a woman.
I walk up to her.
I ask her for the way.
"Excuse me," I say.
"How do I get to the museums?"
The woman smiles kindly.
She points down the large street.
"That is very easy," she says.
"Just go straight ahead here."
"Walk to the end of the street."
"Then turn right."
"The museums are there," she explains.
"Thank you very much," I reply.
I set off and walk straight ahead.
